{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"CVE-2025-3576","state":"PUBLISHED","summary":"A vulnerability in the MIT Kerberos implementation allows GSSAPI-protected messages using RC4-HMAC-MD5 to be spoofed due to weaknesses in the MD5 checksum design. If RC4 is preferred over stronger encryption types, an…","description":"A vulnerability in the MIT Kerberos implementation allows GSSAPI-protected messages using RC4-HMAC-MD5 to be spoofed due to weaknesses in the MD5 checksum design. If RC4 is preferred over stronger encryption types, an attacker could exploit MD5 collisions to forge message integrity codes. This may lead to unauthorized message tampering.","published":"2025-04-15T05:55:26.732Z","lastModified":"2026-09-01T11:51:05.230Z","withdrawn":null,"severity":{"overall":"MEDIUM","cvss":5.9},"cvss":{"v2":null,"v3_0":null,"v3_1":{"vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N","baseScore":5.9,"baseSeverity":"MEDIUM","exploitabilityScore":null,"impactScore":null,"source":"cve.org"},"v4_0":null},"cwe":[{"cweId":"CWE-328","name":"Use of Weak Hash","source":"cve.org"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"Unknown","product":"Unknown","cpe":null,"versions":[{"version":null,"status":"affected","versionEndExcluding":"1.22","versionEndIncluding":null}],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10","cpe":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:10.0","versions":[{"version":"0:1.21.3-8.el10_0","status":"unaffected","versionEndExcluding":"*","versionEndIncluding":null}],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","cpe":"cpe:/o:redhat:enterprise_linux:8::baseos","versions":[{"version":"0:1.18.2-32.el8_10","status":"unaffected","versionEndExcluding":"*","versionEndIncluding":null}],"platforms":[]},{"vendor":"Red Hat","product":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8.2 Advanced Update Support","cpe":"cpe:/o:redhat:rhel_aus:8.2::baseos","versions":[{"version":"0:1.17-19.el8_2.3","status":"unaffected","versionEndExcluding":"*","versionEndIncluding":null}],"pl